1. d4 e6 2. c4 Nf6 3. Nf3 Bb4+ 4. Nbd2 b6 5. a3 Bxd2+ 6. Qxd2 Bb7 7. e3 a5 { black is willing to give up a tempo for this restraining move. However, practice shows that a tempo is more significant here.} 8. b3 d6 9. Be2 Nbd7 10. Bb2 O-O 11. O-O Qe7 12. Rfd1 ({Sokolov won a nice game against Macieja with} 12. Qc2 {- you can find the game annotated as well in this magazine (CBM109).}) 12... Ne4 $6 {this plan is inefficient here: black simply has no time to develop initiative on the kingside} (12... Rfd8 { is more in the spirit of the position} 13. b4 (13. Rac1 c5 14. a4 Rac8 15. Qe1 Nf8 16. Nd2 Ng6 17. f3 e5 { 1/2-1/2 Georgiev,K-Hracek,Z/Plovdiv 2003/CBM 98 no vc (43)}) 13... axb4 14. axb4 Qe8 15. Qc2 Rxa1 16. Bxa1 Ra8 17. Nd2 c5 18. Bc3 Qc8 19. Qb2 h6 { with a slight edge for white. 1-0 Yakovich,Y-Makarov,M/Elista 2001/CBM 83/ 1-0


